<speak>Thank you. I appreciate not having to settle every small thing immediately. At work I spend so much time making quick decisions that I sometimes carry that habit into personal matters. Then I choose something just to remove it from the list, and later I have to revisit it. My nephew has been quite good at slowing me down on office administration. He asks whether we are solving the actual problem or simply clearing the table before the next meeting. I used to find that irritating, but he has a point. A tidy table is nice, but it is not always a tidy process.</speak>